    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/certified-registered-nurse-practitioner-crnp/": {
      "title": "Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP)",
      "description": "Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Student Health Services – Shared Independent Contractor Appointment Chestnut Hill College & Manor College Location: Philadelphia & Jenkintown, PA (On-Site at Both Campuses) Compensation: $60.00–$63.00 per hour, commensurate with experience Schedule: 40 hours per week (20 hours at each institution) Position Summary Chestnut Hill College and Manor College seek an experienced, compassionate, and collaborative Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) to provide comprehensive Student Health Services through a shared independent contractor appointment. This unique opportunity combines direct clinical practice at Chestnut Hill College with clinical and operational leadership at Manor College. The successful candidate will exercise a high degree of clinical autonomy while partnering with campus leaders to promote student wellness, support public health initiatives, and foster healthy campus communities. Services are generally provided during the academic year (August through Commencement), offering an attractive schedule for clinicians seeking alignment with the academic calendar. Position Highlights Chestnut Hill College Serve as the primary clinical provider for Student Health Services, working collaboratively with the Registered Nurse (RN) to deliver comprehensive healthcare services, promote student wellness, and support Student Health Services operations. Manor College Serve as the Director of Student Health Services, providing comprehensive clinical care while leading the day-to-day operations of the health center, wellness initiatives, regulatory compliance, and departmental planning. Primary Responsibilities Provide primary, preventive, urgent, and episodic healthcare services to students. Evaluate, diagnose, treat, and prescribe medications within the CRNP scope of practice. Lead Student Health Services operations at Manor College while collaborating with the Registered Nurse to support operations at Chestnut Hill College. Promote student wellness through health education, prevention, and public health initiatives. Maintain confidential health records and ensure compliance with HIPAA and applicable regulations. Build collaborative partnerships with campus departments, healthcare providers, and community partners. Required Qualifications Active Pennsylvania Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) license with prescriptive authority. Must maintain all professional licenses, certifications, and insurance necessary to perform services as an independent contractor. Successful completion of all required pre-engagement background checks, including criminal history and any other legally required clearances, is required as a condition of appointment. Current CPR/AED certification and other certifications required by law. Professional liability (malpractice) insurance. Experience providing primary healthcare services. Excellent clinical, communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience in college or university Student Health Services. Experience in primary care, ambulatory care, urgent care, or community health. Experience using electronic medical record (EMR) systems. Knowledge of wellness programming, regulatory compliance, or public health initiatives. Why Join Us? Unique opportunity to combine direct patient care with Student Health Services leadership. Serve two collaborative, mission-driven colleges. Exercise significant clinical autonomy in a supportive, student-centered environment. Academic-year schedule (August through Commencement). Competitive independent contractor compensation. Schedule Independent Contractor appointment 40 hours per week: 20 hours at Chestnut Hill College 20 hours at Manor College Services are generally provided during the academic year (August through Commencement). Limited compensated responsibilities outside the academic calendar, including periodic email monitoring and support for enrollment, immunization compliance, accreditation, emergency preparedness, and other mutually agreed-upon institutional needs. Occasional consultation outside of regularly scheduled on-site hours may be required. Approved after-hours consultation services may be invoiced at the agreed-upon hourly rate or, by mutual agreement, offset through adjustments to scheduled on-site service hours during the same workweek. Travel between both campuses is required. To Apply Please submit: Cover Letter Resume or Curriculum Vitae Pennsylvania CRNP license information Contact information for three professional references APPLY HERE Applications will be reviewed immediately and accepted until the position is filled. Chestnut Hill College and Manor College are Equal Opportunity Employers committed to fostering inclusive learning and working environments that support the success and well-being of all students and employees. Explore Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Associate Registrar Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Maternal Child Health (OB Fall 2026) Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon"
