    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/undergraduate-admissions-counselor/": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Undergraduate Admissions Counselor - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Position: Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Reports to: Associate Director of Undergraduate Admissions Department: Undergraduate Admissions Position Summary: The Undergraduate Admissions Counselor serves as a key ambassador for the College, guiding prospective students and families through the admissions process with professionalism, enthusiasm, and care. This role focuses on building meaningful connections, sharing the value of the College’s academic and campus experience, and supporting students from initial inquiry through enrollment. The Counselor represents the institution at recruitment events, both in-person and virtually, and plays an active role in shaping a diverse and engaged incoming class. Success in this position requires strong communication, relationship-building, and problem-solving skills, as well as the ability to think strategically and manage a dynamic schedule that includes travel and participation in events during peak recruitment seasons. About Chestnut Hill College Founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, Chestnut Hill College is an independent, Catholic institution rooted in a strong liberal arts tradition that fosters equality through holistic education. Distinguished by its strong mission, collegial environment, and dedication to personalized instruction through a small faculty-to-student ratio, the College promotes the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person. Located in the charming Chestnut Hill neighborhood of Northwest Philadelphia, CHC serves a culturally diverse student body. Duties & Responsibilities: Manage all activities related to prospective students, applicants, school districts, and colleges from a specific territory/population Attend regional and national college fairs (virtual where applicable) Report on recruitment initiatives, including tracking of inquiries, applications, follow-up contacts, campus visits, etc. that allow for the analysis of enrollment strategies Conduct engagement via telephone, email, written, and personal contact with prospective students, families, and school personnel Conduct file review and information sessions for all populations. Provide campus tours when needed. Promptly respond to phone calls, emails and inquiries Conduct weekly call campaigns and meet high-volume weekly call goals Manage application flow. Evaluate admissions applications and make admission decisions or recommendations in a timely fashion. Assist the financial aid office by providing support during peak times. Work closely with other campus offices to provide information students need to convert acceptances to enrollments Assist with the planning of enrollment related events such as Open House, Admitted Student Days, Group Tours, etc. Extensive travel is required for in-person recruitment to targeted schools, colleges and events in assigned regions to provide presentations to students and parents, including evening and weekend programs. Frequent evening and weekend availability are required. Peak travel seasons: fall and spring. Coordinate special projects as assigned Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college/university. Prior customer service experience Excellent oral and written communication abilities. Engage positively and professionally with diverse groups, fostering strong relationships with prospective students, families, colleagues, and stakeholders. Effectively sell the institution’s value amid higher education difficulties. Proven ability to prioritize multiple tasks, manage deadlines, and stay organized while balancing travel and recruitment duties. Comfortable presenting to large audiences both in-person and virtually. Handle sensitive information with discretion. Meet recruitment targets and deadlines while performing duties off campus (traveling to recruitment events). Strong critical thinking, creativity, and strategic decision-making skills demonstrated through effectively identifying and resolving challenges. Must possess a valid driver’s license, reliable transportation, and car insurance. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the College’s Mission and Core Values, including a shared dedication to inclusive, mission-driven education that supports the development of the whole person. Contact Information: Application Process Interested candidates should submit application materials via ADP Workforce Now HERE. No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Associate Registrar Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Maternal Child Health (OB Fall 2026) Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon"
    },
    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/vice-president-of-enrollment-management-communications/": {
      "title": "Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications",
      "description": "Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications Job Title : Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications Job Location: Philadelphia, PA.  Main Campus Reports to: President Status & Hours: Full-time, Exempt Shift: Primarily Days; Evening & Weekend Hours may be required during peak recruiting Periods Purpose Chestnut Hill College is seeking an accomplished, strategic, and collaborative enrollment leader to serve as Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications. Reporting directly to the President and serving as a member of the President’s Cabinet, the Vice President provides executive leadership for the College’s comprehensive enrollment and communications strategies and is accountable for advancing institutional goals related to recruitment, enrollment, institutional visibility, and net tuition revenue, while partnering with campus leaders to support retention and student success. The Vice President leads an integrated, data-informed approach to enrollment across Undergraduate, Graduate, Transfer, Continuing and Professional Studies, and international populations. The role oversees Admissions, Financial Aid, Global Education, and Marketing and Communications, while partnering closely with Student Success, Academic Affairs, Finance, Student Life, and Information Technology to strengthen the enrollment pipeline, improve student persistence, identify market opportunities, and support the long-term financial sustainability of the College. The successful candidate will be a visible, innovative, and mission-centered leader who can translate enrollment data and market trends into action; build and develop high-performing teams; communicate effectively with diverse constituencies; and bring creativity, urgency, sound judgment, and accountability to the College’s enrollment and communications priorities. About Chestnut Hill College Founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, Chestnut Hill College is an independent, Catholic institution rooted in a strong liberal arts tradition that fosters equality through holistic education. Distinguished by its strong mission, collegial environment, and dedication to personalized instruction through a small faculty-to-student ratio, the College promotes the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person. Located in the charming Chestnut Hill neighborhood of Northwest Philadelphia, it serves a culturally diverse student body. Responsibilities and Essential Duties The Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications will provide strategic and operational leadership in the following areas: Strategic Enrollment Leadership Develop, implement, and assess a comprehensive enrollment management strategy aligned with the College’s mission, academic priorities, financial goals, and long-term sustainability. Collaborate with Student Success and other institutional partners to establish and advance enrollment, retention, and student success goals across Undergraduate, Graduate, Transfer, Continuing and Professional Studies, and international populations. Advise the President and Cabinet on enrollment performance, forecasts, market trends, demographic shifts, risks, opportunities, and competitive positioning. Partner with Academic Affairs and other institutional leaders to identify opportunities for program growth, emerging markets, partnerships, and new student pipelines. Recruitment, Retention, and Student Success Partnership Lead recruitment and admissions strategy across the full enrollment funnel, including inquiry, application, admission, deposit, enrollment, yield, and melt. Direct recruitment marketing and communications strategy, including recruitment messaging, digital outreach, lead generation, market positioning, and communications that effectively articulate College programs and opportunities to prospective students and families. Partner with Student Success, Academic Affairs, Student Life, faculty, and other campus partners to develop and advance institutional retention and student success strategies. Use enrollment, retention, and persistence data to identify trends, opportunities, and areas requiring targeted intervention. Financial, Data, and Operational Management Provide strategic oversight of Financial Aid and partner with Finance on enrollment and net tuition revenue projections, financial aid strategy, affordability, institutional aid utilization, and enrollment mix. Establish a data-informed enrollment culture through forecasting, funnel and yield analysis, dashboards, market research, benchmarking, and performance reporting. Oversee the effective use of CRM and enrollment technologies and collaborate with Information Technology to strengthen data integrity, reporting, automation, and process efficiency. Develop and manage Enrollment Management budgets and evaluate recruitment, marketing, travel, and other investments for effectiveness and return on investment. Leadership and Institutional Collaboration Provide leadership, supervision, coaching, and professional development for Enrollment Management and Communications staff, including leaders responsible for Undergraduate Admissions, Graduate and Accelerated Adult Admissions, Transfer Admissions, Financial Aid, Global Education, Marketing and Communications, and enrollment support functions, while establishing clear performance expectations and accountability. Oversee the College’s broader marketing and communications strategy, including institutional branding, digital communications, public relations, web and social media presence, and other communications that strengthen the College’s visibility and reputation. Facilitate communication and cooperation across Enrollment Management and Communications functions and with academic and administrative units, while representing Enrollment Management and Communications on the President’s Cabinet and with other institutional stakeholders. Ensure enrollment practices are student-centered, operationally effective, and aligned with institutional policies, applicable requirements, and the College’s mission and values. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned by the President. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. A minimum of 10 years of progressive leadership experience in higher education enrollment management, including substantial responsibility for recruitment, admissions, enrollment strategy, and supervision of professional staff. Demonstrated record of developing and executing enrollment strategies and achieving measurable results across multiple student populations and/or academic markets. Knowledge of current best practices in enrollment management, admissions, and retention, and demonstrated experience supporting the success of a diverse student population. Experience with recruitment funnels, enrollment forecasting, data analytics, budget management, strategic marketing and communications, and enrollment technology. Demonstrated knowledge of financial aid strategy and its relationship to enrollment, affordability, institutional aid utilization, and institutional revenue. Strong analytical skills and the ability to translate complex enrollment, market, and financial information into clear recommendations and action plans. Proven ability to lead and develop teams, manage change, establish accountability, and build effective partnerships across organizational boundaries. Excellent interpersonal, written and verbal communication, presentation, problem-solving, and decision-making skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with senior leaders, faculty, staff, students, families, and external partners. Demonstrated professional integrity, discretion, sound judgment, and commitment to the mission and values of Chestnut Hill College. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the College’s Mission and Core Values, including a shared dedication to inclusive, mission-driven education that supports the development of the whole person. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in higher education, enrollment management, business, marketing, public administration, or a related field. Senior-level enrollment leadership experience with responsibility across multiple student populations, including undergraduate, graduate, transfer, adult or continuing education, and international recruitment. Experience using CRM, predictive analytics, digital recruitment, market research, and other contemporary enrollment technologies to improve recruitment and retention outcomes. Demonstrated leadership or oversight of a higher education financial aid function, including familiarity with federal, state, and institutional financial aid requirements. Prior experience in a private, mission-driven, or tuition-dependent higher education environment. Contact Information: Application Process Interested candidates should submit application materials via ADP Workforce Now HERE. No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications Associate Registrar Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Maternal Child Health (OB Fall 2026) Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon"
    },
    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/adjunct-spanish/": {
      "title": "Adjunct",
      "description": "Adjunct - Spanish - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Adjunct – Spanish Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Adjunct – Spanish The Center for Integrated Humanities at Chestnut Hill College in Philadelphia, PA, invites applications for an Adjunct Professor of Spanish beginning in the Spring of 2026. Course Information SPAN 101 – Elementary Spanish I SPAN 102 – Elementary Spanish II SPAN 103 – Intermediate Spanish I On-campus, in-person teaching is preferred, but hybrid teaching may be considered subject to approval by the Office of Academic Affairs. Opportunities for teaching in Fall 2026 (and subsequent semesters) are also available. Requirements Master’s degree (or higher) in Spanish or closely related discipline Previous college-level teaching experience is a plus Exhibited evidence of continued professional growth and development About Chestnut Hill College Chestnut Hill College, founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, is an independent, Catholic institution that strives to foster equality through holistic education within a strong liberal arts tradition.  The mission of the College is dedicated to promoting the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person.  The College, situated in Chestnut Hill, a charming neighborhood in Northwest Philadelphia, serves a culturally diverse student body. Contact Information: Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest, areas of scholarly or clinical interest, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references via ADP Workforce Now HERE .  No phone calls, please. Interviewing will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Official graduate and undergraduate transcripts must also be submitted if granted an interview and hire. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Adjunct – Spanish Associate Registrar Vice President of Enrollment Management & Communications Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Nursing Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Maternal Child Health (OB Fall 2026) Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon"
