    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/academic-advisor-nursing/": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor, Nursing",
      "description": "Academic Advisor, Nursing - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Academic Advisor, Nursing Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Academic Advisor, Nursing Position: Academic Advisor, Nursing Program Department: Center for Nursing Reports to: Director of Nursing Student Success Classification: Exempt / Full-time, 40 Hours Per Week Position Summary The Nursing Academic Advisor for the Nursing Program provides comprehensive academic advising, student-success support, and progression guidance to students enrolled in Chestnut Hill College’s nursing programs. Reporting to the Director of Nursing Student Success, the Advisor works collaboratively with nursing faculty, Student Success, Enrollment Management, the Registrar, Financial Aid, and other College partners to help students navigate academic requirements from enrollment through graduation. The Advisor monitors student progress; identifies potential barriers to persistence, progression, and degree completion; coordinates timely outreach, interventions, and referrals; and serves as a primary resource regarding nursing program requirements, course planning, registration, and College policies. The Advisor refers matters requiring faculty, clinical, or academic judgment to the appropriate nursing leadership. About Chestnut Hill College Founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, Chestnut Hill College is an independent, Catholic institution rooted in a strong liberal arts tradition that fosters equality through holistic education. Distinguished by its strong mission, collegial environment, and dedication to personalized instruction through a small faculty-to-student ratio, the College promotes the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person. Located in the charming Chestnut Hill neighborhood of Northwest Philadelphia, it serves a culturally diverse student body. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Academic Advising & Progression Provide individualized academic advising to an assigned caseload of students enrolled in Chestnut Hill College’s nursing programs. Assist students with academic planning, course sequencing, registration, prerequisites, degree requirements, and program progression expectations. Develop and maintain individualized academic plans that support timely degree completion. Monitor student progress toward graduation and assist students in understanding the academic implications of course withdrawals, unsuccessful course completion, schedule changes, leaves of absence, and other changes affecting their academic plans and progression. Maintain accurate and timely advising notes and student records in accordance with College policies and applicable privacy requirements. Provide clear, consistent guidance regarding College and Nursing Program policies and procedures; refer matters requiring faculty or academic judgment to the appropriate nursing leadership. Student Success & Retention Monitor academic performance, progression milestones, and risk indicators to identify students who may benefit from timely support or intervention. Conduct proactive outreach to students experiencing academic difficulty or other barriers; develop individualized success plans, establish academic goals, and follow up to assess progress and promote continued engagement. Connect students with appropriate campus resources, including Student Success, tutoring, Accessibility Services, Counseling, Financial Aid, Career Development, and other support services. Collaborate with nursing faculty and Student Success staff to address barriers affecting student persistence, progression, academic achievement, and degree completion. Support initiatives that strengthen nursing student retention, engagement, academic achievement, and overall student success. Provide academic support and tutoring in clinical and non-clinical areas of the nursing curriculum, consistent with the Advisor’s areas of expertise. Program Coordination & Collaboration Develop and maintain a strong working knowledge of the College’s nursing curricula, academic requirements, progression standards, and related policies. Collaborate with the Center Chair for Nursing and the Director of Nursing Student Success, nursing faculty, Student Success, the Registrar, Enrollment Management, Financial Aid, and other College offices to resolve student concerns, communicate program requirements, and coordinate timely support. Participate in nursing orientation, registration, admitted student programs, recruitment events, and other student transition activities. In coordination with Enrollment Management, provide admitted students with information regarding nursing curricula, prerequisites, academic expectations, program requirements, and next steps for enrollment and orientation. Support communications to students regarding important deadlines, academic requirements, policy changes, and program information. Maintain accurate documentation of advising interactions, outreach efforts, referrals, and student progression; prepare reports and provide data to support retention efforts, program assessment, accreditation activities, and continuous improvement. Participate in departmental and College meetings, committees, programs, and professional development activities as appropriate. Coordinate with nursing leadership and designated College offices to communicate applicable student requirements related to progression, clinical readiness, compliance documentation, or academic standing; refer determinations and exception requests to the appropriate authority. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in nursing required. Current, unrestricted Registered Nurse (RN) license required. Professional clinical nursing experience required. Minimum of two years of professional experience in academic advising, student success, student services, higher education, counseling, coaching, enrollment services, or a closely related field. Demonstrated commitment to student success and supporting students from diverse backgrounds and educational experiences. Effective interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Excellent organizational, problem-solving, and follow-through capabilities. Demonstrated ability to interpret academic policies, curricula, degree requirements, and student records and communicate information clearly and accurately to students. Ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines, exercise sound judgment, and maintain accurate, confidential student information. Proven success collaborating with faculty, administrators, staff, and students. Proficiency with Microsoft Office or comparable productivity tools and demonstrated aptitude for effectively using student-information, degree-audit, advising, case-management, and early-alert systems. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the College’s Mission and Core Values, including a shared dedication to inclusive, mission-driven education that supports the development of the whole person. Preferred Qualifications Three or more years working in academic advising, student success, retention, or a related higher-education function. Background supporting students in nursing, allied health, health sciences, or another professional academic program. Familiarity with the needs of traditional undergraduate, accelerated, and adult learners. Experience using early-alert, retention, case-management, degree-audit, or academic-progress monitoring systems. Contact Information: Application Process Interested candidates should submit application materials via ADP Workforce Now HERE. No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Academic Advisor, Nursing Academic Advisor, Nursing Director of Financial Aid Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Payroll Coordinator PC/Network Technician Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Adjunct - Music Adjunct - African American History Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon"
    },
    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/director-of-financial-aid/": {
      "title": "Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Director of Financial Aid - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Director of Financial Aid Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Director of Financial Aid Job Description Position: Director of Financial Aid Department: Student Financial Services Reports to: Vice President of Enrollment, Marketing & Communications Classification: Exempt / Full-time, 40 Hours Per Week Purpose The Director of Financial Aid provides strategic leadership and oversight of the College’s financial aid operations, ensuring the effective administration of federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid programs. The Director is responsible for maintaining regulatory compliance, optimizing financial aid systems and processes, and developing strategies that support student recruitment, affordability, retention, and success. The Director leads the Office of Financial Aid, including staff supervision, training, and professional development, while fostering a student-centered approach to financial aid services. Working collaboratively with campus partners, the Director ensures that financial aid policies, practices, and resources align with the College’s enrollment management objectives and institutional priorities. About Chestnut Hill College Founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, Chestnut Hill College is an independent, Catholic institution rooted in a strong liberal arts tradition that fosters equality through holistic education. Distinguished by its strong mission, collegial environment, and dedication to personalized instruction through a small faculty-to-student ratio, the College promotes the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person. Located in the charming Chestnut Hill neighborhood of Northwest Philadelphia, it serves a culturally diverse student body. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide leadership and oversight of the Office of Financial Aid, including staff supervision, training, performance evaluation, and professional development. Direct the administration, awarding, disbursement, and reconciliation of federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid programs. Ensure compliance with applicable federal, state, and institutional regulations, including Title IV requirements, Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP), verification, and Return of Title IV Funds (R2T4). Oversee the preparation and submission of required financial aid reports, including FISAP, IPEDS, audits, and other federal and state reporting requirements. Develop, implement, and maintain financial aid policies, procedures, operational workflows, and student Cost of Attendance (COA) budgets. Monitor financial aid expenditures and allocations, including institutional scholarships, Federal Work-Study funds, and state grant programs. Oversee financial aid management systems, including PowerFAIDS, Jenzabar, COD, NSLDS, and other applicable platforms, ensuring data accuracy, system integration, and operational efficiency. Collaborate with Admissions, Enrollment Management, Student Accounts, Finance, the Registrar, and Information Technology to support institutional goals and streamline financial aid processes. Develop and implement financial aid strategies that support student recruitment, affordability, retention, and enrollment management objectives. Provide guidance to students and families regarding financial aid eligibility, application requirements, financing options, and complex financial circumstances. Monitor changes in financial aid regulations and implement necessary updates to policies, procedures, and systems to ensure continued compliance. Ensure the accuracy, security, and confidentiality of student financial aid records in accordance with FERPA and other applicable regulations. Represent the Office of Financial Aid on institutional committees and participate in admissions events, orientations, and financial aid workshops, including occasional evening and weekend activities. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the College’s mission and strategic priorities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong leadership, supervisory, and decision-making skills, with the ability to develop and support an effective team. Comprehensive knowledge of federal and state financial aid programs, regulations, and compliance requirements. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain complex financial aid information clearly and effectively to students, families, and institutional stakeholders. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills, with exceptional attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and adapt to changing regulations and institutional needs. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and financial aid management systems, preferably PowerFAIDS, Jenzabar, and Informer or InfoMaker. Sound judgment and discretion in handling confidential information and sensitive financial matters. Ability to work independently, exercise initiative, and collaborate effectively across departments. Commitment to providing responsive, student-centered service to individuals from diverse backgrounds. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the College’s Mission and Core Values, including a shared dedication to inclusive, mission-driven education that supports the development of the whole person. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in higher education financial aid administration, including at least three years of supervisory experience. Demonstrated knowledge of federal and state financial aid programs, regulations, and compliance requirements, including Title IV. Eligibility to administer Federal Title IV student financial aid programs in accordance with applicable federal requirements. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in higher education administration, business administration, finance, or a related field. Experience with financial aid management systems, preferably PowerFAIDS and Jenzabar. Contact Information: Application Process Interested candidates should submit application materials via ADP Workforce Now HERE. No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Director of Financial Aid Academic Advisor, Nursing Director of Financial Aid Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Payroll Coordinator PC/Network Technician Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Adjunct - Music Adjunct - African American History Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry"
    },
    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/payroll-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Payroll Coordinator",
      "description": "Payroll Coordinator - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Payroll Coordinator Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Payroll Coordinator Job Title: Payroll Coordinator Job Location: Main Campus Reports to: Controller Status/Hours: Full-Time, Non-Exempt, Permanent Shift: Day, Flexible Chestnut Hill College seeks a Payroll Coordinator to ensure accurate, timely payroll processing, maintain precise financial records, and support compliance with all applicable tax laws and regulations. Purpose The Payroll Coordinator supports a positive employee experience and the College’s financial integrity. This full-time, on-site position offers flexible scheduling and is responsible for payroll administration along with additional accounting-related responsibilities that support the College’s Finance operations. About Chestnut Hill College Chestnut Hill College, founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, is an independent, Catholic institution that strives to foster equality through holistic education within a strong liberal arts tradition. The mission of the College is dedicated to promoting the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person. The College, situated in Chestnut Hill, a charming neighborhood in Northwest Philadelphia, serves a culturally diverse student body. Key Responsibilities Process payroll accurately and on schedule. Maintain employee payroll records, including pay rates, benefits, tax exemptions, overtime, leave, and personal information. Create and manage ADP profiles for new hires; process hire and change paperwork. Generate and analyze payroll and deduction reports, including benefits, garnishments, and retirement contributions. Administer benefit deductions (e.g., medical, dental, life, disability) and reconcile benefits invoices to payroll deductions. Serve as the primary payroll contact for employees; coordinate payroll data with Human Resources and other departments. Prepare payroll journal entries and reconcile monthly payroll liabilities. Track student worker payroll data and reconcile student Federal Work-Study awards and wages in collaboration with the Financial Aid Department to ensure accurate funding allocation and payroll processing. Maintain confidentiality of payroll information and records. Perform additional accounting duties assigned by the Controller or CFO. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the College’s Mission and Core Values, including a shared dedication to inclusive, mission-driven education that supports the development of the whole person. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in business or related field, or equivalent combination of education and payroll/general ledger experience. 3–5 years of payroll processing experience. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and ADP Workforce Now systems. Strong knowledge of federal and state payroll regulations. Excellent organizational, communication, and customer service skills. Ability to work independently, maintain confidentiality, and interact effectively at all organizational levels. Demonstrated ability to work effectively and respectfully with a diverse student body and employee population. Professional, positive, and collaborative approach. Contact Information: Application Process Interested candidates should submit cover letter and resume via ADP Workforce Now HERE. No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Payroll Coordinator Academic Advisor, Nursing Director of Financial Aid Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Payroll Coordinator PC/Network Technician Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Adjunct - Music Adjunct - African American History Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry"
