    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/pc-network-technician/": {
      "title": "PC/Network Technician",
      "description": "PC/Network Technician - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter PC/Network Technician Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities PC/Network Technician Position Title: PC/Network Technician Department: Academic Computing Reports To: Director of Information Technology Position Summary Chestnut Hill College is seeking a knowledgeable, dependable, and service-oriented PC/Network Technician to join its Information Technology team. This position provides technical support to faculty, staff, and students through the installation, configuration, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of computers, network connections, software, and related equipment. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong problem-solving skills, sound judgment, and the ability to work independently while managing multiple priorities. This position requires a proactive approach to technical support, a commitment to excellent customer service, and the ability to collaborate effectively with members of the College community. About Chestnut Hill College Founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, Chestnut Hill College is an independent, Catholic institution rooted in a strong liberal arts tradition that fosters equality through holistic education. Distinguished by its strong mission, collegial environment, and dedication to personalized instruction through a small faculty-to-student ratio, the College promotes the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person. Located in the charming Chestnut Hill neighborhood of Northwest Philadelphia, it serves a culturally diverse student body. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Install, configure, maintain, troubleshoot, and repair desktop computers, laptops, printers, peripherals, and related equipment. Install, update, and troubleshoot Windows operating systems, software applications, hardware drivers, and system utilities. Create, modify, and deactivate user accounts and manage appropriate access permissions in Microsoft Active Directory and Microsoft 365. Install, configure, and troubleshoot network connections and related equipment, including connections within campus wiring closets. Diagnose and resolve hardware, software, connectivity, and security-related issues, including viruses and malware. Monitor and respond to helpdesk requests, voicemail, and email, prioritizing issues and providing timely, professional technical assistance. Maintain accurate helpdesk records, document resolutions, and track outstanding service requests. Provide technical assistance to faculty, staff, and students, including support for campus computer labs and classroom technology. Assist with audiovisual equipment, video production, and technical support for campus events as needed. Coordinate with vendors and external technical support providers to resolve equipment and software issues. Assist with equipment inventory, organization, maintenance, and the coordination of student workers as appropriate. Exercise sound independent judgment in troubleshooting technical issues, determining appropriate solutions, and escalating complex matters when necessary. Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Associate degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Minimum of two years of experience in computer support, networking, or a related technical field. Working knowledge of Microsoft Windows operating systems, Microsoft 365, Active Directory, and basic networking concepts. Experience troubleshooting computer hardware, software, peripheral devices, and network connectivity. Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills with attention to detail. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, take initiative, and manage competing priorities with minimal supervision. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with a demonstrated commitment to responsive and professional customer service. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive institutional information appropriately. Availability to work occasional evenings and weekends to support campus events, system maintenance, and other operational needs. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the College’s Mission and Core Values, including a shared dedication to inclusive, mission-driven education that supports the development of the whole person. Preferred Qualifications CompTIA A+, Microsoft, or other relevant technical certifications. Previous IT support experience in a higher education environment. Familiarity with Windows Server, helpdesk ticketing systems, and audiovisual technology. Contact Information: Application Process Interested candidates should submit application materials via ADP Workforce Now HERE. No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore PC/Network Technician Academic Advisor, Nursing Director of Financial Aid Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Payroll Coordinator PC/Network Technician Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Adjunct - Music Adjunct - African American History Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry"
    },
    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/adjunct-african-american-history/": {
      "title": "Adjunct",
      "description": "Adjunct - African American History - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Adjunct – African American History Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Adjunct – African American History Position: Adjunct, African American History Department: Academic Affairs Reports to: Vice President of Academic Affairs Status: Exempt / Part-time Adjunct Purpose The Center for Integrated Humanities and History department at Chestnut Hill College in Philadelphia, PA, are seeking an adjunct lecturer to teach HIST-248 African Americans after Emancipation in the Spring 2027 semester. On-campus, in-person teaching is preferred. Opportunities for teaching survey courses in African American history as well as courses in the applicant’s area of expertise may be available in subsequent semesters. The History Department provides a true holistic education with a focus on collaborative and interactive learning. Class sizes are small and students are expected to produce evidence of critical thinking and integrated learning on essay exams, papers, and oral presentations. The History faculty at CHC, who bring a variety of historical backgrounds to their instruction, develop one-on-one relationships with their students. They are available to help students and guide them when necessary, and actively listen to and engage with all students. About Chestnut Hill College Founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, Chestnut Hill College is an independent, Catholic institution rooted in a strong liberal arts tradition that fosters equality through holistic education. Distinguished by its strong mission, collegial environment, and dedication to personalized instruction through a small faculty-to-student ratio, the College promotes the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person. Located in the charming Chestnut Hill neighborhood of Northwest Philadelphia, it serves a culturally diverse student body. Qualifications Ph.D. in History or African American Studies (ABDs will be considered). Expertise in African American history (eighteenth, nineteenth, or twentieth century). Thematic specialty is open. Previous college teaching experience is a plus. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the College’s Mission and Core Values, including a shared dedication to inclusive, mission-driven education that supports the development of the whole person. Contact Information: To apply: Interested candidates should submit application materials via ADP Workforce Now HERE . No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Adjunct – African American History Academic Advisor, Nursing Director of Financial Aid Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Payroll Coordinator PC/Network Technician Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Adjunct - Music Adjunct - African American History Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Student