    "https://www.chc.edu/careers-at-chc/employment-opportunities/adjunct-music/": {
      "title": "Adjunct",
      "description": "Adjunct - Music - Chestnut Hill College Skip to main content Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Search Icon Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Search Icon Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics Academic Centers Degrees and Programs Student Support Services Career Development Meet the Faculty Student Life Clubs and Programs Student Leadership Career Development Health, Wellness, and Fitness Safety and Security Athletics About Chestnut Hill College Celebrates 100 Years Welcome From the President Mission Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion History and College Seal Faculty & Staff Directory Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Parents and Families Alumnae/i Faculty & Staff Directory Quicklinks News & Publications Events Event Rentals Careers at CHC Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Adjunct – Music Home Careers at CHC Employment Opportunities Adjunct – Music Job Title: Music Adjunct Job Location: Main Campus Department: Academic Affairs Reports to: Vice President of Academic Affairs Classification: Exempt/Part-time Chestnut Hill College invites applications for an adjunct faculty position in Music starting in the Spring 2027 semester. The successful candidate will primarily be responsible for directing an undergraduate instrumental ensemble, with additional teaching assignments possible based on departmental needs and the candidate’s areas of expertise. The Music Adjunct will provide engaging, student-centered instruction that fosters students’ musical proficiency, artistic growth, and academic development while supporting the mission and educational goals of Chestnut Hill College. About Chestnut Hill College Founded by the Sisters of Saint Joseph in 1924, Chestnut Hill College is an independent, Catholic institution rooted in a strong liberal arts tradition that fosters equality through holistic education. Distinguished by its strong mission, collegial environment, and dedication to personalized instruction through a small faculty-to-student ratio, the College promotes the spiritual, academic, social, ethical, and moral development of the whole person. Located in the charming Chestnut Hill neighborhood of Northwest Philadelphia, it serves a culturally diverse student body. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Direct and provide instruction for an undergraduate instrumental ensemble in accordance with established course objectives and program expectations. Develop and implement instructional materials, rehearsal plans, and learning activities appropriate to the ensemble and students’ levels of musical proficiency. Establish clear expectations, assess student performance, and provide constructive, timely feedback. Foster a respectful, inclusive, and collaborative learning environment that accommodates varying levels of musical experience and ability. Utilize appropriate instructional methods, technologies, and resources to enhance student learning and musical development. Maintain accurate attendance, academic records, and communication with students regarding course requirements and progress. Actively recruit student musicians for participation in the instrumental ensemble through College Open Houses, campus events, and off-campus outreach opportunities. Collaborate with Music Program faculty, Humanities Center leadership, and other members of the College community to support program activities and initiatives. Participate in meetings and activities related to ensemble instruction, recruitment, and performance. Perform other duties consistent with the adjunct teaching assignment, as appropriate. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Music, Music Education, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Candidates with significant professional experience and demonstrated expertise in a specialized area of music may also be considered, as appropriate to the teaching assignment. Demonstrated proficiency and experience in directing instrumental ensembles. Ability to deliver effective, engaging instruction to students with varying levels of musical experience and ability. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Ability to collaborate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and other members of the College community. Ability to fulfill instructional responsibilities and meet established academic deadlines. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the College’s Mission and Core Values, including a shared dedication to inclusive, mission-driven education that supports the development of the whole person. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience at the college or university level. Professional experience in instrumental performance, ensemble conducting, music education, or a related discipline. Experience recruiting, developing, and leading student instrumental ensembles. Experience working with undergraduate students from diverse academic, cultural, and musical backgrounds. Familiarity with instructional technology and learning management systems. Contact Information: To apply: Interested candidates should submit a Curriculum Vitae and a brief statement of teaching philosophy via ADP Workforce Now HERE . No phone calls, please. Chestnut Hill College is an employer committed to a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion as a core value.  To foster an inclusive community and support our diverse student body, we embrace equal access. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and encourage applications from groups historically underrepresented in higher education.  We are committed to increasing the diversity of the college community and the curriculum. Chestnut Hill College is an equal opportunity employer Explore Adjunct – Music Academic Advisor, Nursing Director of Financial Aid Financial Systems Analyst - Student Financial Services Payroll Coordinator PC/Network Technician Financial Aid Counselor Certified Registered Nurse Practitioner (CRNP) Center Chair, Nursing Assistant Athletic Trainer, Fulltime (10 Months) Direct Support Professional - Life Skills through Career Program Clinical Nursing Adjunct - Medical Surgical Adjunct - Spanish Adjunct - Music Adjunct - African American History Instructor - Computer and Information Sciences Adjunct - Computer Programming Assistant Professor/Instructor of Cybersecurity (Faculty/ 9 Months) 9601 Germantown Ave Philadelphia, PA 19118 215-248-7000 Contact Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Twitter Menu Resources Prospective Students Current Students Alumnae/i Parents and Families Faculty & Staff Directory Policies and Reports Center for Accessibility and Learning Services Careers at CHC Web Accessibility Discover Admissions & Aid Academics Student Life Neurodiversity Initiative Athletics CHC Bookstore Quick Links Safety and Security Directions and Parking News & Publications Events Comms Request Form myCHC Email Office 365 Logue Library Canvas IT Help Desk Resources Also of Interest Consumer Information Campus Crisis Protocols and Closing Information Giving Societies Ways to Give Related Pages Health and Wellness Apply to Chestnut Hill College Campus Ministry Apply Visit Info Alumni Give Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Student Admissions Accelerated Adult Students Tuition and Financial Aid Academics 